This project has a graphify knowledge graph at `graphify-out/`.
The CLI is the project venv: `./.venv-graphify/bin/graphify` (not a global `graphify` on PATH).

## When to use graphify (required)

Run graphify **before** Read/Grep/Glob when the task needs cross-file or architectural context:

- "How does X work?", data flow, or dependency tracing
- Finding callers, usages, or relationships you do not already know
- Exploring an unfamiliar area of the codebase
- Broad refactors touching many modules
- Subagents doing exploration — include this rule in their prompt

Commands:
- `./.venv-graphify/bin/graphify query "<question>"` — scoped subgraph (add `--budget 1500` to cap output)
- `./.venv-graphify/bin/graphify path "<A>" "<B>"` — shortest path between two concepts
- `./.venv-graphify/bin/graphify explain "<concept>"` — all nodes related to a concept

If `graphify-out/wiki/index.md` exists, prefer it over reading scattered raw files for orientation.

## When to skip graphify (go direct)

Do **not** run graphify when the task is already scoped — use Read/Grep/Glob directly:

- User named a specific file or path ("in `FooController.php`", "line 42 of …")
- Single-file or few-line edits (fix, rename, format, add a method)
- Config/tooling only (`composer.json`, CI, env, git, PR, commit)
- Running a known command or test the user specified
- Debugging a specific error at a known stack trace location
- Follow-up after graphify already oriented you — read only the lines you need to edit

## Other

- Read `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` only for broad architecture review when query/path/explain are not enough.
- After modifying code files, run `./.venv-graphify/bin/graphify update .` to keep the graph current (AST-only, no API cost).
- If `graphify-out/graph.json` does not exist yet, explore normally or build the graph first.
